COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[375,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nRead the story of people of Shu'ayb from more than one surah in the Holy Quran and reflect on its lessons.\nShare a message in which you advise a fellow Muslim using a Quranic verse.\nStudy a text in Arabic with the intention of comprehending the Book of Allah, the Almighty.\nguid\nWarn those around you with what you memorize and comprehend from the Holy Quran.\nDeath of the heart makes one rules out the coming of punishment.\nNo matter how long and enjoyable someone's life is, it will not avail him from reckoning and recompense.\nrefl\nفَأَسۡقِطۡ عَلَيۡنَا كِسَفٗا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ١٨٧ قَالَ رَبِّيٓ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ ١٨٨ فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَخَذَهُمۡ عَذَابُ يَوۡمِ ٱلظُّلَّةِۚ\nThis is what they asked for when they asked for a part of heaven to fall upon them. Allah made their punishment in the form of intense heat which overwhelmed them for seven days, and nothing could protect them from it. Then He sent a cloud to shade them, so they ran toward it to seek its shade from the heat. When all of them had gathered underneath it, Allah sent sparks of fire, flames and intense heat upon them, and caused the earth to convulse beneath them, and He sent against them a mighty blast that destroyed their souls. Ibn Kathir: 3/335.\nThe Punishment of people of Shu'ayb was what they asked for. Explain.\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكۡثَرُهُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٩٠\nOne may ask: Why is the above-mentioned verse repeated after every story? The answer is: It is more assertive in taking heed, and alerting to the hearts. Moreover, each story is an independent narration on its own, hence, each ends with the same as the next one. Ibn Juzay: 2/123.\nWhy is the above-mentioned verse repeated after every story?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَتَنزِيلُ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٩٢\nThe One Who sent it down is the Originator of the heavens and the earth, Who sustains the entire universe, both the upper and lower realms. As He cared for them by guiding them to what is in their best interests in worldly terms and their physical well-being, He also cares for them by guiding them to what leads to well-being in religious terms and in the hereafter. One of the greatest signs of His care for them is the sending down of this noble Book that contains much goodness and abundant blessings. In it, there is guidance to that which is in people’s best interests in this world and the Hereafter, and righteous manners and attitudes that is not found in any other book. Al-Saadi: 597-598.\nWhat is learned from describing Allah in this verse as (the Lord of the worlds)?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَتَنزِيلُ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٩٢ نَزَلَ بِهِ ٱلرُّوحُ ٱلۡأَمِينُ ١٩٣ عَلَىٰ قَلۡبِكَ لِتَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُنذِرِينَ ١٩٤ بِلِسَانٍ عَرَبِيّٖ مُّبِينٖ ١٩٥\nThink about how these sublime virtues were combined in this noble Book. For it is the best of books, brought down by the best of the angels, to the best of mankind, to the best part of him -namely his heart- to the best nation brought forth for mankind, in the best, most eloquent and richest of languages, namely clear Arabic tongue. Al-Saadi: 598.\nDescribe the virtues of the Holy Quran.\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَكُن لَّهُمۡ ءَايَةً أَن أَن يَعۡلَمَهُۥ عُلَمَٰٓؤُاْ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ ١٩٧\nWith regard to anything about which there is confusion, the matter should be referred to people of experience and knowledge, so that their word may be proof against others, just as the magicians who were highly skilled in the area of magic confirmed that the miracles of Moses were true and were not magic. After that, no attention is to be paid to the words of the ignorant. Al-Saadi: 598.\nThe knowledge of the scholars of Children of Israel is considered enough evidence of the truthfulness of this Quran. Why?\nفَيَقُولُواْ هَلۡ نَحۡنُ مُنظَرُونَ ٢٠٣\nMeaning: So that we believe and accept. They will wish to go back to worldly life and given respite. Al-Baghawi: 3/373.\nWhat will the denier wish for when he witness the punishment?\nأَفَرَءَيۡتَ إِن مَّتَّعۡنَٰهُمۡ سِنِينَ ٢٠٥\nMeaning: The time length of their respite will not benefit them if it is followed by punishment, even if the respite is long, since every awaited event is near. Ibn Juzay: 2/124.\nDoes a long lifetime benefit a person if he continues to commit sins?\nwords\nوَالجِبِلَّةَFormer creation, nations of people\nالمُسَحَّرِينَThose affected by magic\nكِسَفًاFragments of torment\nالظُّلَّةِA cloud that shaded them, then burned them\nزُبُرِ الأَوَّلِينَThe Scriptures of previous Prophets\nالأَعجَمِينَThose who do not speak Arabic"],[376,"§Ash-Shu'ara\ndeeds\nCollaborate with some of your relatives in making a preaching program to benefit your relatives with good words and likable gifts.\nPerform nighttime prayer, and prolong your prostration.\nRemember Allah, the Almighty, using open and assigned Athkar, such as saying: (Glorified is Allah and praised is He) as many as a hundred times, and Asking for Allah’s forgiveness as many as seventy times.\nguid\nWhoever invokes other than Allah, will be punished after death.\nA preacher will reach success only through forbearance, modesty, and leniency with others.\nBeware of wrongdoing others, remember its consequence on its doers, and reflect on those around you who transgressed and tyrannized, then were decimated by Allah.\nrefl\nمَآ أَغۡنَىٰ عَنۡهُم مَّا كَانُواْ يُمَتَّعُونَ ٢٠٧\nAllah says: Then, came to them the punishment of which We warned them for disbelieving Our verses, and denying Our Messenger. (Shall not avail them), the lengthy life and pleasures We gave them did not avail them, since they did not repent. The pleasures of life did not benefit them; in fact, they ruined them, and increased their sins and crimes, which would not have happened had they not had these pleasures. Al-Tabari: 19/402.\nA long life without good deeds leads to demise and punishment. Explain.\nفَلَا تَدۡعُ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَٰهًا ءَاخَرَ فَتَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُعَذَّبِينَ ٢١٣\nThis was addressed to the Prophet (ﷺ) despite the fact that it was inconceivable that shirk would occur from him (ﷺ), but it was a motivation toward more sincerity. In essence, it means: \"Be sincere in the Oneness of Allah until you see none with Him.\" Moreover, this verse indicates to all people that shirk is so evil and bad that even those who would never do it are forbidden from it. Al-Alusi: 10/131.\nWhat the benefit of forbidding the Prophet (ﷺ) from committing shirk despite the fact that it was inconceivable to occur from him?\nوَأَنذِرۡ عَشِيرَتَكَ ٱلۡأَقۡرَبِينَ ٢١٤\nThis does not contravene the command to warn all people, because if a person is instructed to be kind to all people, then it is said to him: Be kind to your relatives, this is emphasizing the importance of kindness to relatives and highlighting the fact that they have a particular right to that. Al-Saadi: 599.\nIs it understood from this verse that the Prophet’s (ﷺ) message was limited to his people?\nوَٱخۡفِضۡ جَنَاحَكَ لِمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢١٥ فَإِنۡ عَصَوۡكَ فَقُلۡ إِنِّي بَرِيٓءٞ مِّمَّا تَعۡمَلُونَ ٢١٦\nThis is in order to avoid giving the wrong impression to one who may misunderstand and think that the words (And lower your wing in kindness to the believers) imply approving of everything that they do, so long as they are believers. This notion is warded off by this verse. Al-Saadi: 599.\nThis term: (If they disobey you) comes after this: (And lower your wing in kindness to the believers). Why?\nوَتَقَلُّبَكَ فِي ٱلسَّٰجِدِينَ ٢١٩\nMeaning: Allah sees you praying with others, which indicates the importance of the prayer in congregation. Ibn Juzay: 2/124.\nThis verse indicates the prayer in congregation. How?\nيُلۡقُونَ ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَأَكۡثَرُهُمۡ كَٰذِبُونَ ٢٢٣\n(They pass), they receive what is heard. It is said that it means the devils who pass what they hear to the monks; or it means the soothsayers who pass what they hear to the public. (And most of them are liars), the devils, or the soothsayers , since they lie in what they tell about the devils. Ibn Juzay: 2/125.\nWhere did the lies of the soothsayers and fortunetellers come from?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّهُمۡ فِي كُلِّ وَادٖ يَهِيمُونَ ٢٢٥\nMeaning: They engage in vain talk, and do not trace the ways of truth, since whoever followed the truth and knew that he would be held accountable for what he says, he would ascertain the accuracy of his words, and would never wander aimlessly in every subject with recklessness. Al-Qurtubi: 16/95.\nWhat do you say about one who indulges with others in every subject, engages in vain talk, and does not follow the truth?\nwords\nالسَّمعِEavesdrop on heaven\nلَمَعزُولُونَThey are barred and pelted by flames\nوَاخفِض جَنَاحَكَBe gentle and speak softly with modesty\nأَفَّاكٍA liar\nأَثِيمٍSinful\nوَادٍEverything of lie and falsehood\nيَهِيمُونَThey wander aimlessly\nمُنقَلَبٍFinal return"],[377,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nEstablish prayers at the mosque, in a humble manner, and fulfill its requirements and sunnah acts.\nGive charity to someone in need.\nSupplicate Allah by His names, (the All-Knowing) and (the All-Wise) to grant you knowledge, wisdom, and memorization of the Quran.\nguid\nAffirming the inimitability of the Quran, for its verses consists of letters such as Ta-Seen, Ha-Meem, yet the creation could not produce the like of it.\nEstablish prayer properly with its pillars, requirements, conditions, and in a humble manner to be able to benefit from the verses of the Quran.\nDenying resurrection and the Hereafter makes the denier the worst among creation, even worse than livestock.\nrefl\nهُدٗى وَبُشۡرَىٰ لِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢ ٱلَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَيُؤۡتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ\nPerhaps it may be said that there are many who claim to believe, so should this be accepted from everyone who claims to be a believer? Or is it essential that there should be evidence? This is true that there should be evidence, therefore, Allah describes the characteristics of the believers: (Who establish prayer). Al-Saadi: 601.\nWhat is the sign of truthfulness of one who claims to believe?\nوَهُم بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمۡ يُوقِنُونَ ٣\nTheir certainty of the Hereafter entails that they should strive fully for it; moreover, Allah warns them against the causes that lead to punishment, which is the basis of all good. Al-Saadi: 601.\nWhat does certainty of the Hereafter entail?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ زَيَّنَّا لَهُمۡ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَهُمۡ يَعۡمَهُونَ ٤\nThese deeds contain apparent and hidden shirk, and since the disbelievers are accustomed and addicted to these deeds, they become unable to receive the guidance of this Book. Ibn Ashur: 19/220.\nIn view of this verse, explain the consequence of insisting on sin.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ زَيَّنَّا لَهُمۡ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَهُمۡ يَعۡمَهُونَ ٤\n(Indeed, for those who do not believe), they do not establish, nor resume the belief. (In the Hereafter, We have made pleasing), With Our power that cannot be fended off. (To them their deeds), clearly wicked deeds that they ignored to think about their consequences. Al-Biqai: 14/127.\nWhat is the consequence of having weak faith in the Hereafter?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ زَيَّنَّا لَهُمۡ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَهُمۡ يَعۡمَهُونَ ٤\nThe devil makes their deeds appealing to them by whispering, which they find acceptable, as Allah narrates about him, (By Your Glory, I will surely mislead them all ` Except, among them, Your chosen servants) [38:82-83]. The present tense of the verb (wander) indicates their continuous blindness without the possibility of returning to the truth, because they believe that they are right. Note that the continuity of this blindness varies in intensity; the worst of it may extend until death, while in other cases, it may be shorter than that commensurate with the extent of the appealing of disbelief in their souls. Ibn Ashur: 19/221.\nThis verse indicates one of the approaches of the devil to mankind. What is it?\nوَأَلۡقِ عَصَاكَۚ فَلَمَّا رَءَاهَا تَهۡتَزُّ كَأَنَّهَا جَآنّٞ وَلَّىٰ مُدۡبِرٗا وَلَمۡ يُعَقِّبۡۚ يَٰمُوسَىٰ لَا تَخَفۡ إِنِّي لَا يَخَافُ لَدَيَّ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلُونَ ١٠\nAllah says, (In My presence) to make him feel safe, since he Messengers, among all people, fear Allah the most. Allah says, (Only the people of knowledge among His servants fear Allah) [35:28]. There are none more knowledgeable about Allah than the Messengers. Al-Alusi: 10/159.\nAllah says, (In My presence). Why?\nيَٰمُوسَىٰ لَا تَخَفۡ إِنِّي لَا يَخَافُ لَدَيَّ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلُونَ ١٠ إِلَّا مَن ظَلَمَ ثُمَّ بَدَّلَ حُسۡنَۢا بَعۡدَ سُوٓءٖ فَإِنِّي غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ١١\nOne may say: What is the meaning of fear after repentance and forgiveness? It should be said that this is the way of those who have knowledge about Allah; they are in constant fear of their sins, and always feel apprehensive about not fulfilling the conditions of repentance. Al-Qurtubi: 16/330.\nWhy do the righteous fear their sins after asking for Allah's forgiveness?\nwords\nيَعمَهُونَThey wander blindly in their evil deeds\nلَتُلَقَّىYou are receiving\nمِن لَدُنFrom\nآنَستُI have spotted\nبِشِهَابٍA burning torch\nتَصطَلُونَYou may warm yourselves\nمُبصِرَةًClear and visible"],[378,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nRecall three blessings, bestowed upon you by Allah, then thank Him for them, following the example of the Prophets.\nReflect on the life of ants, or listen to a science documentary on it, then write three useful lessons your learned.\nSay, [My Lord, inspire me to be grateful for Your favor which You have bestowed upon me and my parents, and to do righteous deeds that please you. And admit me, by Your mercy, among Your righteous servants]\nguid\nShare your smiles when it is appropriate, and beware of constant frowning.\nThank Allah when He blesses one or both of your parents; for any blessing given to the parent is a blessing to the son, offering thanks and gratitude is among the reasons for the continuity of blessings.\nWhoever is entrusted by Allah with any matter, he must, out of fear of Him, take good care of what he has been entrusted with.\nrefl\nفَٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ١٤\nThe point is: Beware, O you who disbelieve in Muhammad and deny the Message that he has brought from his Lord, lest the same thing that befell them befall you also, since Muhammad (ﷺ) is nobler and greater than Moses, and his proof is stronger than that of Moses. Ibn Kathir: 3/345-346.\nThis verse warns against disbelieving in Muhammad (ﷺ) while its subject is about those disbelieved in Moses. Explain.\nوَقَالَا ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي فَضَّلَنَا عَلَىٰ كَثِيرٖ مِّنۡ عِبَادِهِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٥\nThis is a sign of a person being blessed: That he is grateful to Allah for His bounty, both spiritual and worldly, and he sees all blessings from his Lord, but he does not boast about them, and he is not filled with self-admiration because of them. Rather, he sees that this requires him to give a great deal of thanks. Al-Saadi: 602.\nIn light of this verse, explain the effect of blessings on righteous people.\nوَوَرِثَ سُلَيۡمَٰنُ دَاوُۥدَۖ\nMeaning: He inherited him in kingship and Prophethood. What is meant here is not wealth, because if that were the case, Solomon would not have been singled out from among the sons of David, for the wealth of the Prophets cannot be inherited. Ibn Kathir: 3/346.\nFaith, knowledge, and wisdom are the best thing a son inherits from his father. Explain in light of this verse.\nفَتَبَسَّمَ ضَاحِكٗا مِّن قَوۡلِهَا\nAl-Zajjaj said: Most of the Prophet's laughter is smiling, hence, laughter means smiling. Al-Baghawi: 3/391.\nHow was the laughter of the Prophets (p)?\nوَتَفَقَّدَ ٱلطَّيۡرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِيَ لَآ أَرَى ٱلۡهُدۡهُدَ أَمۡ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡغَآئِبِينَ ٢٠ لَأُعَذِّبَنَّهُۥ عَذَابٗا شَدِيدًا أَوۡ لَأَاْذۡبَحَنَّهُۥٓ أَوۡ لَيَأۡتِيَنِّي بِسُلۡطَٰنٖ مُّبِينٖ ٢١\nThis verse proves the duty of the ruler in taking notice of his subjects, and looking after them. Seeing how the hoopoe, despite its tiny size, did not scape the notice of Solomon, then, how about what is bigger than that. May Allah have mercy on Omar bin Al-Khattab (t) who followed Solomon’s example when he said: “If a goat at the bank of Euphrates is taken by a wolf, Omar will be questioned about it.” Al-Qurtubi: 16/131.\nIs becoming head of state an honor and privilege, or a duty and responsibility that the person will be questioned about it? Explain in view of this verse.\nلَأُعَذِّبَنَّهُۥ عَذَابٗا شَدِيدًا أَوۡ لَأَاْذۡبَحَنَّهُۥٓ أَوۡ لَيَأۡتِيَنِّي بِسُلۡطَٰنٖ مُّبِينٖ ٢١\nMeaning: A clear reason for his absence. This is indicative of his perfect piety and fairness; he did not simply swear to punish or kill him, because that could only be in the case of committing a sin, and there could have been a clear excuse for his absence. Therefore, he made this exception, because of his piety and discernment. Al-Saadi: 604.\nThis verse indicates Solomon's piety, and prudence. How?\nفَمَكَثَ غَيۡرَ بَعِيدٖ فَقَالَ أَحَطتُ بِمَا لَمۡ تُحِطۡ بِهِۦ وَجِئۡتُكَ مِن سَبَإِۢ بِنَبَإٖ يَقِينٍ ٢٢\nThis incident proves that the weakest creature may achieve something that the strongest cannot. Hence, scholars should belittle their knowledge and attribute the knowledge of everything to Allah. Moreover, this refutes the claim by Shia that nothing is hidden from their Imam, and that no one is more knowledgeable than him. Al-Biqai: 14/150.\nDespite Solomon's (u) wide knowledge and kingdom, the hoopoe knew what he did not. What does that indicate?\nwords\nيُوزَعُونَThey march in organized ranks\nأَوزِعنِيInspire me\nسَبَإٍSheba, a city in Yemen"],[379,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nIf you receive any news today, ascertain the truth; for it is a Quranic approach that is not overlooked by the righteous.\nDenounce any wrongdoing you see in your neighborhood as did that hoopoe when it witnessed shirk.\nGive gifts to those whom you seek their guidance to the truth, as this approach softens the hearts.\nguid\nThe wise knows the weakness of a woman, hence he does not push her into doing unsuitable work for her.\nRemember that satan beautifies evil deeds to those who are heedless of remembrance of Allah, and avert servants from the way of Allah.\nWhen authoring books, sermons, and letters, it is best to preface with the Basmalah.\nrefl\nإِنِّي وَجَدتُّ ٱمۡرَأَةٗ تَمۡلِكُهُمۡ وَأُوتِيَتۡ مِن كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ وَلَهَا عَرۡشٌ عَظِيمٞ ٢٣ وَجَدتُّهَا وَقَوۡمَهَا يَسۡجُدُونَ لِلشَّمۡسِ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَصَدَّهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ فَهُمۡ لَا يَهۡتَدُونَ ٢٤\nAbu Bakrah (t) said: When Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was informed that the Persians had crowned the daughter of Khosrau as their ruler, he said, \"Such people as ruled by a lady will never be successful.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/499.\nDraw a useful lesson from this verse.\nأَلَّاۤ يَسۡجُدُواْۤ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي يُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡخَبۡءَ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا تُخۡفُونَ وَمَا تُعۡلِنُونَ ٢٥\nMeaning: They worship the One, who alone, has the Perfection, by prostrating to Him, which is an expression of nearness, a circle of communion, and a sign of healing. If they prostrate to Allah, they will be guided, since prayer restrains one from immorality and wrongdoing; hence, the devil would be unable to misguide them. Al-Biqai: 14/152-153.\nWhat is the effect of prostrating to Allah on man’s life?\n۞قَالَ سَنَنظُرُ أَصَدَقۡتَ أَمۡ كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلۡكَٰذِبِينَ ٢٧\n(Whether you were truthful or were of the liars), this indicates that the ruler should accept the excuses of his subjects, and spare them his punishment, since Solomon did not punish the hoopoe after providing an explanation for its absence. The hoopoe’s honesty became its excuse. Al-Baghawi: 3/459.\nVerification of claims is one of the sunnah of Prophets. Explain in view of this verse.\nقَالَتۡ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلۡمَلَؤُاْ أَفۡتُونِي فِيٓ أَمۡرِي مَا كُنتُ قَاطِعَةً أَمۡرًا حَتَّىٰ تَشۡهَدُونِ ٣٢\nThis verse was taken as evidence for consulting others, and soliciting views on important matters. Al-Alusi: 10/192.\nHow do you handle important matters?\nإِنَّهُۥ مِن سُلَيۡمَٰنَ وَإِنَّهُۥ بِسۡمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ٣٠\nThis shows that it is encouraged to begin one’s letters by quoting the Basmalah (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) in full. Al-Saadi: 604.\nWhat is encouraged at the beginning of writing?\nوَإِنِّي مُرۡسِلَةٌ إِلَيۡهِم بِهَدِيَّةٖ فَنَاظِرَةُۢ بِمَ يَرۡجِعُ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلُونَ ٣٥\nQatadah said: \"May Allah have mercy on her and be pleased with her, how wise she was as a Muslim and (before that) as an idolator! She understood how gift-giving has a good effect on people.\" Ibn Abbas and others said: \"She said to her people, if he accepts the gift, he is a king, so fight him; but if he does not, then, he is a Prophet, so follow him.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/350.\nDealing with matters wisely lead to guidance. Explain in view of this verse.\nوَإِنِّي مُرۡسِلَةٌ إِلَيۡهِم بِهَدِيَّةٖ فَنَاظِرَةُۢ بِمَ يَرۡجِعُ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلُونَ ٣٥\nIn essence, she said to her people: I am testing this man with an expensive gift; if he was a worldly king, he would be satisfied, but if was a Prophet, then he would be satisfied only when we accept his religion; then she sent him a great gift. Ibn Juzay: 2/130.\nHow did the queen of Sheba know the truthfulness of Solomon (u)? What do you learn from her action?\nwords\nالخَبءَWhat is hidden\nالمَلأُEminent ones\nتَعلُوا عَلَيَّYou become arrogant toward me\nأَفتُونِيAdvise me\nقَاطِعَةً أَمرًاI would decide a matter\nتَشهَدُونِYou witness me\nأُولُوWe have, are\nفَنَاظِرَةٌI shall wait"],[380,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nWrite a message in which you explain the risk of preferring this worldly life over religion.\nGive a talk or share a message in which you warn against dealing in bribery.\nRecall three favors, bestowed upon you by Allah, then thank Him for them so that He would bless them for you.\nguid\nThe standards of those who seek the Hereafter are different from that of those who seek this worldly life, and that is why they do not rejoice in the life of this world.\nKnow that the greatest of all blessings is faith, not this transient worldly life, which a true believer does not incline toward it.\nReflect on the combination of these two of Allah’s attributes: Freedom from need and Generosity.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ سُلَيۡمَٰنَ قَالَ أَتُمِدُّونَنِ بِمَالٖ فَمَآ ءَاتَىٰنِۦَ ٱللَّهُ خَيۡرٞ مِّمَّآ ءَاتَىٰكُمۚ\nThe queen of Sheba considered the acceptance or rejection of her gift as a sign of what she was thinking of Solomon, whether he was a king or a Prophet since he said to her in his letter: (Do not be arrogant towards me, but come to me in full submission). This demand cannot be rescinded by taking a ransom or accepting a gift. Sharia has made accepting gifts lawful, even desirable; however, in this case, this was similar to bribing and trading truth for falsehood, which is unlawful to accept. Al-Qurtubi: 16/159.\nWhy did Solomon (u) reject the gift?\nبَلۡ أَنتُم بِهَدِيَّتِكُمۡ تَفۡرَحُونَ ٣٦\nMeaning: You rejoice in what is gifted to you because of your focus on worldly life only, and desire for more of it. This is a scathing rebuke to them. Al-Alusi: 10/195.\nThe preacher to truth and guidance should not be deluded by this life's ornament. How do you infer this meaning from the verse?\nقَالَ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلۡمَلَؤُاْ أَيُّكُمۡ يَأۡتِينِي بِعَرۡشِهَا\nAbu Jaafar said: The best possible explanation for Solomon singling out her throne to be brought to him from among the rest of her kingdom is to make its transfer as a proof of his Prophethood, and to show her some effects of Allah’s might and power. She kept her throne in a secure cell inside a locked house, but Allah took it out without breaking locks or opening doors, and delivered it to His ally (Solomon). This was the greatest proof of the truthfulness of his Prophethood and of what he was calling her to. Al-Tabari: 19/463.\nAmong the rest of her kingdom, Solomon singled out her throne to be brought to him. Why?\nقَالَ عِفۡرِيتٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡجِنِّ أَنَا۠ ءَاتِيكَ بِهِۦ قَبۡلَ أَن تَقُومَ مِن مَّقَامِكَۖ وَإِنِّي عَلَيۡهِ لَقَوِيٌّ أَمِينٞ ٣٩ قَالَ ٱلَّذِي عِندَهُۥ عِلۡمٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ أَنَا۠ ءَاتِيكَ بِهِۦ قَبۡلَ أَن يَرۡتَدَّ إِلَيۡكَ طَرۡفُكَۚ فَلَمَّا رَءَاهُ مُسۡتَقِرًّا عِندَهُۥ قَالَ هَٰذَا مِن فَضۡلِ رَبِّي لِيَبۡلُوَنِيٓ ءَأَشۡكُرُ أَمۡ أَكۡفُرُۖ\nThis debate between the powerful jinn and the one who had knowledge from the Scripture indicates that knowledge and wisdom can achieve what power cannot. Ibn Ashur: 19/271.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of knowledge and wisdom. How?\nفَلَمَّا رَءَاهُ مُسۡتَقِرًّا عِندَهُۥ قَالَ هَٰذَا مِن فَضۡلِ رَبِّي لِيَبۡلُوَنِيٓ ءَأَشۡكُرُ أَمۡ أَكۡفُرُۖ\n(This is from the favor of my Lord), it is a pure favor from Allah upon me without merit or an effort from my side ordained by Allah. Al-Alusi: 10/199.\nThe greatest way to thank Allah for a blessing is to attribute it to Him. Explain in light of this verse.\nفَلَمَّا رَءَاهُ مُسۡتَقِرًّا عِندَهُۥ قَالَ هَٰذَا مِن فَضۡلِ رَبِّي لِيَبۡلُوَنِيٓ ءَأَشۡكُرُ أَمۡ أَكۡفُرُۖ\n(This is from the favor of my Lord to test me whether I will be grateful or ungrateful), it is a test or trial for me. He was not deceived by his dominion, authority and power, as usually happens with ignorant kings; rather, he knew that this was a test from his Lord, and he was afraid that he would not thank Him for this blessing. Then, he explained that gratitude does not benefit Allah; rather, it benefits the one who shows gratitude, as he said: (Whoever is grateful, his gratitude is to his own benefit, and whoever is ungrateful, then indeed, my Lord is Free of need and most generous). Al-Saadi: 605.\nWhat is the main difference between righteous and ignorant kings?\nوَمَن شَكَرَ فَإِنَّمَا يَشۡكُرُ لِنَفۡسِهِۦۖ وَمَن كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ رَبِّي غَنِيّٞ كَرِيمٞ ٤٠\n(And whoever is grateful - his gratitude is only for [the benefit of] himself), the benefit of being grateful is solely to himself, since it would increase the blessing and sustain it. Gratitude is the keeper of an existing blessing, and bringer of a missing one. (And whoever is ungrateful - then indeed, my Lord is Free of need) of his gratitude, and (generous) by bestowing His blessings upon those who are ungrateful. Al-Baghawi: 3/404.\nWhat is the benefit of being grateful to Allah for His blessings?\nwords\nصَاغِرُونَThey will be debased\nعِفرِيتٌA powerful jinn\nنَكِّرُواDisguise\nالصَّرحَThe palace\nمُمَرَّدٌIt is made smooth\nمِن قَوَارِيرَFrom clear glass"],[381,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you explain that the ruling on regarding anything as a bad omen is not limited to movements of birds, but extends to everything one feels pessimistic about.\nMemorize the supplication that discourages pessimism, which is: “O Allah, there is no portent other than Your portent, no goodness other than Your goodness, and none worthy of worship other than You.”\nSupplicate Allah that the outcome of disbelievers’ plots against Muslims become their own destruction.\nguid\nThe believer is always optimistic, because good omen brings only good, which is a perfect sign of having full trust in Allah.\nRemember that whoever plans against others, Allah will plan against him and the bad consequence will backfire on him.\nOur certainty is firmly anchored in Allah's support and protection of his Allies.\nrefl\nقَالُواْ ٱطَّيَّرۡنَا بِكَ وَبِمَن مَّعَكَۚ قَالَ طَٰٓئِرُكُمۡ عِندَ ٱللَّهِۖ بَلۡ أَنتُمۡ قَوۡمٞ تُفۡتَنُونَ ٤٧\n(He said, \"Your omen is from Allah), whatever befalls of good or bad is with Allah, and is decreed by Him, and when any fate is decreed by Allah, it happens very swiftly. Al-Baghawi: 3/407.\nFate happens very swiftly. Why?\nقَالُواْ ٱطَّيَّرۡنَا بِكَ وَبِمَن مَّعَكَۚ قَالَ طَٰٓئِرُكُمۡ عِندَ ٱللَّهِۖ بَلۡ أَنتُمۡ قَوۡمٞ تُفۡتَنُونَ ٤٧\nA bad omen is harmful to one’s thinking and destructive to his plans. Whoever thinks that a lowing of a cow, or croaking of a raven prevents fate or ward off destiny, is ignorant. Al-Qurtubi: 16/181.\nExplain the risk of a bad omen to a person.\nقَالُواْ ٱطَّيَّرۡنَا بِكَ وَبِمَن مَّعَكَۚ قَالَ طَٰٓئِرُكُمۡ عِندَ ٱللَّهِۖ بَلۡ أَنتُمۡ قَوۡمٞ تُفۡتَنُونَ ٤٧\n(We consider you and those who are with you as a bad omen) - they claimed that they did not see any sign of good in Salih's face and that he and the believers with him had become a cause of some harm that befell their worldly interests. So, Salih said to them: (Your omen is from Allah), it only befell you because of your sins, (but you are a people who are being tested) with ease and hardship, good and bad, to see whether you will give up sin and repent, or not. Al-Saadi: 606.\nWhat are the reasons for accidents and afflictions that strike a person?\nوَمَكَرُواْ مَكۡرٗا وَمَكَرۡنَا مَكۡرٗا وَهُمۡ لَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٥٠\nAllah called their conspiracy a (plan), since it was a harmful ploy done in private. Ibn Ashur: 19/284.\nIn this verse, the conspiracy is called a (plan), why?\nفَتِلۡكَ بُيُوتُهُمۡ خَاوِيَةَۢ بِمَا ظَلَمُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٥٢\nThis verse proves that wrongdoing is a cause for ruining houses. Ibn Abbas said: \"In the Book of Allah, I found that wrongdoing ruins the houses,\" then, he recited this verse. In the Torah: \"O son of Adam, do not wrong others, lest your house would be ruined.\" It is said that this indicates the demise of the wrongdoer since the ruining of his house entails his own destruction. It is widely known that wrongdoing as transgressing and violating the rights of Allah's servants is a cause for ruining houses, as it is seen often at present times. Al-Alusi: 10/209.\nWhat are the worst consequences of wrongdoing?\nفَتِلۡكَ بُيُوتُهُمۡ خَاوِيَةَۢ بِمَا ظَلَمُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٥٢\nTheir disbelief enticed them to commit many sins, such as spreading corruption, however, Allah singles out their wrongdoing, because of its effect in ruining their dwellings. Ibn Ashur: 19/285.\nAmong the reasons for the punishment of Thamud, the verse mentions only their wrongdoing. Why?\nوَلُوطًا إِذۡ قَالَ لِقَوۡمِهِۦٓ أَتَأۡتُونَ ٱلۡفَٰحِشَةَ وَأَنتُمۡ تُبۡصِرُونَ ٥٤\nMeaning: This repulsive deed that is abhorrent to sound minds and sound human nature, and it is regarded as abhorrent according to the teachings of all religions. Al-Saadi: 607.\nThe crime of Lot's people is called immorality. Why?\nwords\nاطَّيَّرنَاWe consider you as a bad omen\nطَائِرُكُم عِندَ اللهِYour omen, good or bad, is with Allah\nتَقَاسَمُواThey took mutual oath\nلَنُبَيِّتَنَّهُWe will kill him by night\nخَاوِيَةًDesolate"],[382,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to make you love belief and adorn your heart with it, and make you hate disbelief, deviance, and rebellion.\nSupplicate Allah often today by saying: \"Our Lord, let our spouses and children be a source of joy for us, and make us good examples for the righteous.\"\nIdentify one of your needs, and supplicate Allah, the Almighty, persistently to ease it for you.\nguid\nWhen wrongdoers lose an argument, they resort to force.\nWhen someone is addicted to committing a sin, it does not become hideous to him.\nSaving his allies and destroying his enemies is an affirmed way of Allah.\nrefl\n۞فَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُوٓاْ أَخۡرِجُوٓاْ ءَالَ لُوطٖ مِّن قَرۡيَتِكُمۡۖ إِنَّهُمۡ أُنَاسٞ يَتَطَهَّرُونَ ٥٦\nThe punishment is implied in their last statement, for they are the people who said: (Drive the family of Lot out of your town, for they are a people who keep themselves pure), what this implies is: \"You are immersing yourselves in evil and filth, which dictates that the punishment will befall your city, and that those who leave will be saved.\" Al-Saadi: 607.\nThe statement of the people of Lot was the cause for their destruction. Explain.\nفَأَنجَيۡنَٰهُ وَأَهۡلَهُۥٓ إِلَّا ٱمۡرَأَتَهُۥ قَدَّرۡنَٰهَا مِنَ ٱلۡغَٰبِرِينَ ٥٧\nMeaning: She was one of those who were destroyed, with her people, because she was a helper to what they did, and she approved of their evil deeds. She told them about the guests of Lot so that they could come to them. She did not do the evil deeds herself, which was because of the honor of the Lot (u) and not because of any honor on her part. Ibn Kathir: 3/356.\nWhy was Lot's wife destroyed? How did she subscribe to what her people were doing?\nقُلِ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ وَسَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰ عِبَادِهِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱصۡطَفَىٰٓۗ ءَآللَّهُ خَيۡرٌ أَمَّا يُشۡرِكُونَ ٥٩\nAfter praising Allah, the Prophet (ﷺ) was enjoined to say greeting of peace upon the Messengers who preceded him as a tribute to them for their strive in spreading the true religion. Ibn Ashur: 20/6.\nAfter praising Allah, the Prophet (ﷺ) was enjoined to say greeting of peace upon the Messengers. Why?\nأَمَّن جَعَلَ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ قَرَارٗا وَجَعَلَ خِلَٰلَهَآ أَنۡهَٰرٗا وَجَعَلَ لَهَا رَوَٰسِيَ وَجَعَلَ بَيۡنَ ٱلۡبَحۡرَيۡنِ حَاجِزًاۗ أَءِلَٰهٞ مَّعَ ٱللَّهِۚ بَلۡ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٦١\nThis is a great arrangement, and no one can grasp this amazing design until he realizes that this earth is moving through space constantly; nevertheless, it appears still to its inhabitants, which is even more amazing. This arrangement is a blessing and mercy, since if it were not still, people would be in shock and chaos, where nothing can be accomplished. Ibn Ashur: 20/13.\nHow can we realize Allah's great arrangement for the earth?\nوَجَعَلَ بَيۡنَ ٱلۡبَحۡرَيۡنِ حَاجِزًاۗ أَءِلَٰهٞ مَّعَ ٱللَّهِۚ بَلۡ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٦١\n(And made a barrier between two flowing bodies of water), the salty water and the fresh water; He has placed a barrier between them to prevent the two types of water mixing, which would cause the benefits of each to be lost. Al-Saadi: 608.\nWhy is there a barrier between two flowing bodies of water?\nأَمَّن يُجِيبُ ٱلۡمُضۡطَرَّ إِذَا دَعَاهُ وَيَكۡشِفُ ٱلسُّوٓءَ وَيَجۡعَلُكُمۡ خُلَفَآءَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ أَءِلَٰهٞ مَّعَ ٱللَّهِۚ قَلِيلٗا مَّا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٦٢\nThe reason for responding to the desperate is his sincere turn toward Allah, and his abandonment of everything else. Allah informs us of his acceptance of the invocation of those who turn sincerely to Him, even if they were disbelievers; He says, (until when you are in the ships and they sail with those on board and rejoicing in a favorable wind, then suddenly a stormy wind comes, with waves crashing into them on all sides, and they feel that there is no escape. Then they cry out to Allah with sincere devotion to Him, \"If You save us from this, we will surely be among those who are grateful\") [10:22]. And says, (When they board a ship, they supplicate Allah, devoting their faith sincerely to Him. But as soon as He rescues them to the land, they associate partners with Him) [29:65]. So, Allah responded to them in their distress and sincerity, despite His knowledge that they will go back to their shirk. Al-Shawkani: 4/169.\nWhat is the reason for Allah’s answer to the supplication of the desperate despite his disbelief?\nأَمَّن يُجِيبُ ٱلۡمُضۡطَرَّ إِذَا دَعَاهُ وَيَكۡشِفُ ٱلسُّوٓءَ وَيَجۡعَلُكُمۡ خُلَفَآءَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ أَءِلَٰهٞ مَّعَ ٱللَّهِۚ قَلِيلٗا مَّا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٦٢\nAllah insures his response to the desperate, and He says so about Himself. The reason for that is the distress which induces sincerity to Him only, and abandonment of everything else. This sincerity is significant in the sight of Allah, whether it comes from a believer or a disbeliever, an obedient or a sinner. Al-Qurtubi: 16/193.\nExplain the outcome of the sincere supplication of Allah, the Almighty.\nwords\nقَدَّرنَاهَاWe destined Lot's wife\nالغَابِرِينَThose who remained in punishment\nذَاتَ بَهجَةٍDelightful beauty\nيَعدِلُونَThose who ascribe equals to Allah\nخِلاَلَهَاIn its midst\nرَوَاسِيَFirm mountains"],[383,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nGive advice to those who search for the unseen through the stars or fortune tellers.\nRead and reflect on the demise of wrongdoers.\nRecall five blessings, bestowed upon you by Allah, then thank Him for them .\nguid\nknowledge of the unseen is exclusive to Allah, so whoever claims that he knows the unseen, is nothing but a liar.\nDisbelieving in the Hereafter makes the servant have the audacity to commit sins.\nFollowing the guidance of the Quran protects against differing and disputing.\nrefl\nقُل لَّا يَعۡلَمُ مَن فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ ٱلۡغَيۡبَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُۚ وَمَا يَشۡعُرُونَ أَيَّانَ يُبۡعَثُونَ ٦٥\nThe preceding verses nullify the divinity of the polytheists' idols through clear proofs, and the creed of shirk is abolished, then comes this verse to eliminate one of the remnants of shirk, which was the claim to know the unseen through divination and words from jinn. Ibn Ashur: 20/19.\nThese verses eliminate one of the remnants of shirk. What is it?\nبَلِ ٱدَّٰرَكَ عِلۡمُهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۚ بَلۡ هُمۡ فِي شَكّٖ مِّنۡهَاۖ بَلۡ هُم مِّنۡهَا عَمُونَ ٦٦\nHere Allah relates the situation of these disbelievers that they do not know when the Hereafter will come, then He discloses that their knowledge of the Hereafter is weak, then, He says that they are in doubt concerning it, rather they are blind to it, then He affirms that they deny it, and think it is unlikely to happen. Because of these doubts, fear of the Hereafter left their hearts; as a result, they had the audacity to disobey Allah, and it became easy for them to deny the truth and believe in falsehood, so they indulged in their physical desires, and kept away from worshiping Allah. Thus, they lost out both in this world and in the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 609.\nWhat made the disbelievers have the audacity to commit sins?\nقُلۡ سِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَٱنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ ٦٩\nAllah warned them through the example of previous denying nations, and commanded His Prophet to enjoin them to travel the land and see the ruins of these wicked nations, and take heed. Ibn Atiyah: 4/269.\nWhat is the benefit of reading about the wicked and their history?\nوَلَا تَحۡزَنۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا تَكُن فِي ضَيۡقٖ مِّمَّا يَمۡكُرُونَ ٧٠\nThe Prophet's (ﷺ) mercy and compassion for his people was overwhelming, hence he was moved by this warning to his people, therefore, Allah strengthened his heart by encouraging him not to grieve over them if they are punished. Ibn Ashur: 20/26.\nThis verse indicates the Prophet's (ﷺ) mercy toward his people. How?\nقُلۡ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَكُونَ رَدِفَ لَكُم بَعۡضُ ٱلَّذِي تَسۡتَعۡجِلُونَ ٧٢ وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُو فَضۡلٍ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَشۡكُرُونَ ٧٣\nThis is a special news for the Prophet (ﷺ), indicating that the delayed punishment is an effect of Allah's mercy, since a delayed time is a respite to them, which is a blessing for them. Ibn Ashur: 20/28.\nDelaying the punishment is an effect of Allah's mercy. Explain.\nوَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَيَعۡلَمُ مَا تُكِنُّ صُدُورُهُمۡ وَمَا يُعۡلِنُونَ ٧٤\nThis verse reveals that they had more disgraceful actions than what was told about them. The word (conceal) comes first to indicate that concealing and declaring are the same to Allah's knowledge, or what is hidden inside is the reason for what appears on the outside. Al-Alusi: 10/228.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning the concealed knowledge first? How do you infer from this verse the importance of hearts’ deeds?\nإِنَّ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ يَقُصُّ عَلَىٰ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلَّذِي هُمۡ فِيهِ يَخۡتَلِفُونَ ٧٦\nMeaning: Had they believed in this Quran, it would explain to them that over which they differ. Al-Qurtubi: 16/204.\nWhen we differ over a particular matter, where can we find the answer?\nwords\nوَمَا يَشعُرُونThey do not know\nأَيَّانَWhen\nادَّارَكَTheir knowledge cannot comprehend its time\nعَمُونَThey are blind to it\nأَسَاطِيرُ الأَوَّلِينَLegends of the former people\nرَدِفَ لَكُمIt came near you\nتُكِنُّIt conceals"],[384,"§An-Naml\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to make the Holy Quran a testimony and a mercy for you.\nListen to a lecture or a sermon, then practice what you heard.\nSleep early one night, then go sleep late on another, and compare the difference between these two nights on your mentality, health, work, and worship.\nguid\nAmong the objectives of the holy Quran are guidance and mercy for mankind.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, Allah will judge justly between people on every dispute they have in this life.\nIt is a duty on every Muslim and a student of knowledge not to speak about any issue of which he has no knowledge until the truth becomes clear to him. So, he speaks only based on knowledge.\nrefl\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٧٧\nThe Quran is a mercy to the believers, because when they become guided by it, they attain the triumph in this life by having reformed souls, righteous deeds, and being united; and the triumph in the Hereafter, which is Paradise. Ibn Ashur: 20/31.\nThe Quran is a mercy to the believers. How?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٧٧\nThe believers are singled out for mention here, even though it is a mercy to the worlds, since the believers are the ones who benefit from it. Al-Alusi: 10/229.\nThe believers are singled out for mention here, even though it is a mercy to the worlds. Why?\nفَتَوَكَّلۡ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّكَ عَلَى ٱلۡحَقِّ ٱلۡمُبِينِ ٧٩\n(You are upon the clear truth), and for the one who is on the path of clear truth - calling people to it and supporting it - it is more appropriate that he should rely upon Allah. For he is striving concerning a matter that is definitely sound, and is known to be true, concerning which there is no doubt or confusion. Al-Saadi: 609.\nHow is reliance upon Allah related to the Prophet (ﷺ) being on the clear truth?\nإِنَّكَ لَا تُسۡمِعُ ٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰ وَلَا تُسۡمِعُ ٱلصُّمَّ ٱلدُّعَآءَ إِذَا وَلَّوۡاْ مُدۡبِرِينَ ٨٠\n(Indeed, you will not make the dead hear), the disbelievers, since they abandoned reflection, so they are like the dead who have no senses or minds. (Nor will you make the deaf hear the call), the disbelievers who are like the deaf, since whenever they are called to what is good, they turned away as if they did not hear. Al-Qurtubi: 16/205.\nThe disbelievers are described as (dead) and (deaf). Why?\nوَوَقَعَ ٱلۡقَوۡلُ عَلَيۡهِم بِمَا ظَلَمُواْ فَهُمۡ لَا يَنطِقُونَ ٨٥\nQatadah said: \"How will they speak when they have no valid argument?\" Al-Baghawi: 3/418.\nWhy will they be speechless?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٨٦\nMeaning: \"I decreed that their faith is constantly renewed, so they are elevated higher every day.\" Al-Biqai: 14/222.\nThe verb (believe) is in the present tense form. What does that indicate?\nصُنۡعَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَتۡقَنَ كُلَّ شَيۡءٍۚ إِنَّهُۥ خَبِيرُۢ بِمَا تَفۡعَلُونَ ٨٨\nThere is a wisdom in everything created by Allah, as He says, (It is the work of Allah, who perfected all things), and says, (Who perfected everything He created)[32:7]. Allah, the Almighty, is in no need of the worlds. So, His wisdom consists of two parts, first: A wisdom that belongs to Him, which He likes and approves. Second: A blessing upon His servants, which makes them joyful and happy. Ibn Taimyah: 5/68.\nThere is a wisdom in everything created by Allah. Explain what this wisdom consist of.\nwords\nوَلَّوا مُدبِرِينَThey turned away\nفَوجًاA group\nيُوزَعُونَThey are driven in rows\nدَاخِرِينَThey are fully humbled\nجَامِدَةًMotionless\nتَمُرُّIt moves"],[385,"§An-Naml, Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nPerform a good deed, and ask Allah to multiply its reward for you .\nRead a Surah from the Holy Quran with reflection and comprehension.\nSay, \"O Allah! show me the truth as true, and inspire me to follow it; and show me falsehood as falsehood, and inspire me to abstain from it.\"\nguid\nYour safety from the terror of the Day of Resurrection consummate with your performance of good deeds in this life.\nA mere listening to the recital of the Holy Quran may become a reason for a servant's guidance, if Allah wills.\nOne of Allah's ways is to destroy wrongdoers when they deal arrogantly with reformers, divide their unity, or strive to weaken or kill them.\nrefl\nمَن جَآءَ بِٱلۡحَسَنَةِ فَلَهُۥ خَيۡرٞ مِّنۡهَا وَهُم مِّن فَزَعٖ يَوۡمَئِذٍ ءَامِنُونَ ٨٩\n(Will be rewarded with better than it), Allah's reward will be much better than the servant's deeds, words, and remembrance. Moreover, the pleasure from Allah with the servant will be greater than his deed. This is due to the multiplication of reward, as Allah will reward him ten times as much as his deed, and will grant him an eternal bliss for his belief during his short worldly life. Al-Qurtubi: 16/224.\nWhat is the meaning of: (Will be rewarded with better than it)?\nوَأَنۡ أَتۡلُوَاْ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَۖ فَمَنِ ٱهۡتَدَىٰ فَإِنَّمَا يَهۡتَدِي لِنَفۡسِهِۦۖ\n(And to recite the Quran), I, constantly, read it to the people by repeatedly calling others to it, because of its efficacy in guiding people to the right way. It is said: I read it persistently to unravel the hidden truths between its lines, little by little. Al-Alusi: 10/248.\nWhat is the effect of constantly reading the Holy Quran?\nوَمَن ضَلَّ فَقُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُنذِرِينَ ٩٢\nMeaning: I have an example to follow in the Messengers who warned their people, and did what they had to do in order to convey the Message to them, and fulfil the covenant they had made. Allah will judge their nations to whom they were sent. Ibn Kathir: 3/366.\nWhat is the duty of the warners toward the misguided?\nنَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡكَ مِن نَّبَإِ مُوسَىٰ وَفِرۡعَوۡنَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ لِقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٣\n(For people who believe). It is addressed to them, for they have the faith to focus and reflect on it, which would prompt them to accept it and learn from it, so that they will learn from it and be guided, and it will increase them in faith and certainty, adding goodness to their goodness. As for others, they will not benefit from it except in the sense that proof will be established against them. Allah has protected the Quran from them, and made a barrier between them and the Quran, so that they will not understand it. Al-Saadi: 611.\nThis narration is for those who believe. Why?\nإِنَّ فِرۡعَوۡنَ عَلَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ\nPharaoh eminence in this worldly life is described as (exalted himself in the land) in order for the lesson in his demise to become the most notable of all lessons. Ibn Ashur: 20/66.\nPharaoh's eminence in this worldly life is described as: (exalted himself in the land). Why?\nإِنَّ فِرۡعَوۡنَ عَلَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَجَعَلَ أَهۡلَهَا شِيَعٗا\n(Factions), groups; where each one followed and supported something different from the other, but they were all under Pharaoh’s command and control like weak pieces of wood. He divided them, lest they unite against him, then he would not gain what he wanted from them. Hence, they became divided, not protecting, rather forsaking each other until they hit bottom. Al-Biqai: 14/240.\nDividing people is always among the objectives of the enemies. What is the effects of division on the power of the nation?\nيُذَبِّحُ أَبۡنَآءَهُمۡ وَيَسۡتَحۡيِۦ نِسَآءَهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ٤\nPharaoh did that because the priests said to him: A newborn from the Children of Israel will destroy your kingdom. It is said that the fortune tellers told him that, or it was an interpretation of a dream he saw. Al-Zajjaj said: \"How foolish Pharaoh was! He did not realize that if the priest was telling the truth, then killing newborns would be of no avail, and if the priest was lying, then the killing would be pointless.\" Al-Qurtubi: 16/230.\nDescribe Pharaoh's foolishness.\nwords\nبِالحَسَنَةِGood deeds: Monotheism, belief, worship\nبِالسَّيِّئَةِBad deeds: Shirk, disbelief\nحَرَّمَهَاMade it sacred; no blood shedding, no hunting and no cutting of its trees or bushes\nعَلاَHe became an arrogant tyrant\nشِيَعًاFactions\nنَمُنَّWe confer favor"],[386,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nSend a message to a family whose one of its members was wronged, and give them a glad tidings of this verse.\nAsk Allah, the Almighty, to make your wife and offsprings a source of joy to you.\nAsk Allah, the Almighty, to reassure your heart, and keep you firm in times of prosperity and adversity.\nguid\nEstablishment in the land requires patience, preparation, and making efforts.\nA blessing may come with hardship. Allah promised Moses’ mother, during her extreme hardship, of relief and a great blessing, which was making her son a Prophet.\nMaintaining patience during times of hardships is a favor from Allah, so, ask Him to grant you that.\nrefl\nوَأَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَىٰٓ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنۡ أَرۡضِعِيهِۖ فَإِذَا خِفۡتِ عَلَيۡهِ فَأَلۡقِيهِ فِي ٱلۡيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحۡزَنِيٓۖ إِنَّا رَآدُّوهُ إِلَيۡكِ وَجَاعِلُوهُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٧\nThis indicates that Allah inspires the believers with faith and what is beneficial to them by prompting them, even if they are not Prophets. Ibn Taimyah: 5/70.\nThe verse shows Allah's favor upon the believers. Explain.\nوَأَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَىٰٓ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنۡ أَرۡضِعِيهِۖ فَإِذَا خِفۡتِ عَلَيۡهِ فَأَلۡقِيهِ فِي ٱلۡيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحۡزَنِيٓۖ إلى قوله تعالى وَقَالَتۡ لِأُخۡتِهِۦ قُصِّيهِۖ\nEven if a person knows that the divine will and decree and the promise of Allah will inevitably come to pass, he should not neglect to take proper measures as Allah has instructed, and that is not contrary to faith in the promise of Allah. Allah promised the mother of Moses that He would return her son to her, yet she took measures to bring him back, and she sent his sister to track him down, and find out where he was. Al-Saadi: 619.\nMoses' mother sent his sister to track him down. Does that contradict her belief in Allah's promise?\nوَأَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَىٰٓ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنۡ أَرۡضِعِيهِۖ فَإِذَا خِفۡتِ عَلَيۡهِ فَأَلۡقِيهِ فِي ٱلۡيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحۡزَنِيٓۖ إِنَّا رَآدُّوهُ إِلَيۡكِ وَجَاعِلُوهُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٧\nShe was ordered to nurse him so he would be fit and content with his mother's milk. Moreover, this last nursing would strengthen him before being cast into the river, giving him energy to last him until he would be picked up by Pharaoh's family and taken to Pharaoh's palace. Ibn Ashur: 20/73.\nMoses' mother was ordered to nurse him before casting him into the river. Why?\nوَقَالَتِ ٱمۡرَأَتُ فِرۡعَوۡنَ قُرَّتُ عَيۡنٖ لِّي وَلَكَۖ لَا تَقۡتُلُوهُ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَنفَعَنَآ أَوۡ نَتَّخِذَهُۥ وَلَدٗا وَهُمۡ لَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٩\nThe presence of righteous people among corruptors alleviates the intensity of corruption. Pharaoh's wife was a reason for averting Pharaoh from killing the child despite of him being an Israelite. Ibn Ashur: 20/86.\nThe presence of the righteous among corruptors alleviates corruption intensity. Explain.\nعَسَىٰٓ أَن يَنفَعَنَآ أَوۡ نَتَّخِذَهُۥ وَلَدٗا\nAllah decreed that he should be a source of benefit to the wife of Pharaoh who said these words, for when he became a source of joy to her, and she loved him dearly, he continued to be like a loving son toward her, until he grew up, and Allah made him a Prophet and a Messenger. Then she hastened to submit and believe in him. May Allah be pleased with her and make her pleased. Al-Saadi: 612.\nDid Pharaoh’s wife benefit from her compassion toward Moses?\nوَأَصۡبَحَ فُؤَادُ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ فَٰرِغًاۖ إِن كَادَتۡ لَتُبۡدِي بِهِۦ لَوۡلَآ أَن رَّبَطۡنَا عَلَىٰ قَلۡبِهَا لِتَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٠\nIf , when calamity befalls a person, he remains patient and steadfast, his faith increases thereby. This indicates that continuing to be panic-stricken is a sign of weakness of faith. Al-Saadi: 613.\nWhat is the link between becoming panic-stricken and the level of faith?\nوَأَصۡبَحَ فُؤَادُ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ فَٰرِغًاۖ إِن كَادَتۡ لَتُبۡدِي بِهِۦ لَوۡلَآ أَن رَّبَطۡنَا عَلَىٰ قَلۡبِهَا لِتَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٠\nIt is said that her heart was devoid of everything except the thought of Moses. Ibn Taimyah: 5/70.\nMother’s love for her children is immense. Explain in view of this verse.\nwords\nاليَمِّThe river Nile\nقُرَّةُ عَينٍ لِيA source of joy for me\nفَارِغًاEmpty from everything except Moses (u)\nلَتُبدِي بِهِShe was about to disclose about him\nيَكفُلُونَهُ لَكُمThey will rear and nurse him for you"],[387,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nReconcile between two feuding individuals.\nRecall a sin you had committed, and ask for Allah's forgiveness, saying, \"My Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me.\"\nSupport a righteous person by defending him against wrongs written about him in newspaper, internet, or messages.\nguid\nDo good in your worship, and Allah will give you wisdom and knowledge.\nBeware of the devil, for he is an enemy and a deceiver to the children of Adam.\nTaking initiative to provide good to people, and giving advice to them are part of doing good.\nrefl\nوَلَمَّا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُۥ وَٱسۡتَوَىٰٓ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ حُكۡمٗا وَعِلۡمٗاۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١٤\n(And this is how We reward those who do good) by worshiping Allah and treating His creation with kindness. We give them knowledge and wisdom commensurate with their good deeds, and this is indicative of Moses' (u) high level of perfection in doing good. Al-Saadi: 613.\nThe verse indicates the great reward for doing good. Explain.\nقَالَ هَٰذَا مِنۡ عَمَلِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِۖ إِنَّهُۥ عَدُوّٞ مُّضِلّٞ مُّبِينٞ ١٥\nThis proves that human soul is based on good, which is the true nature of mankind. Deviating from good requires unnatural cause, which is the infiltration of satan's temptation into human soul. Ibn Ashur: 20/90.\nIn view of this verse, what is the basic nature of human soul?\nوَدَخَلَ ٱلۡمَدِينَةَ عَلَىٰ حِينِ غَفۡلَةٖ مِّنۡ أَهۡلِهَا فَوَجَدَ فِيهَا رَجُلَيۡنِ يَقۡتَتِلَانِ هَٰذَا مِن شِيعَتِهِۦ وَهَٰذَا مِنۡ عَدُوِّهِۦۖ فَٱسۡتَغَٰثَهُ ٱلَّذِي مِن شِيعَتِهِۦ عَلَى ٱلَّذِي مِنۡ عَدُوِّهِۦ فَوَكَزَهُۥ مُوسَىٰ فَقَضَىٰ عَلَيۡهِۖ قَالَ هَٰذَا مِنۡ عَمَلِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِۖ إِنَّهُۥ عَدُوّٞ مُّضِلّٞ مُّبِينٞ ١٥\n(Causing his death), he killed him, nevertheless, Moses (u) did not mean to kill the Egyptian, but his fist coincided with the appointed death time for the Egyptian, so he died, which made Moses regretful, and saw that it was satan's stirring his hand, and the anger he felt was tempted by satan. He admitted to what happened, and called it \"satan's work.\" Moses physical strength may contributed to the killing unintentionally. Ibn Atiyah: 4/280.\nMoses attributed the killing of the Egyptian to satan despite the fact that he did it. Why?\nقَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي ظَلَمۡتُ نَفۡسِي فَٱغۡفِرۡ لِي فَغَفَرَ لَهُۥٓۚ\nHe admitted wronging himself by committing an unauthorized offense against someone else. Ibn Taimyah: 5/71.\nAdmission of guilt is a trait of Prophets. Explain.\nقَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي ظَلَمۡتُ نَفۡسِي فَٱغۡفِرۡ لِي فَغَفَرَ لَهُۥٓۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ١٦\nThen, he admitted his guilt and asked for Allah's forgiveness, and Allah forgave him. If it said: Why did he ask for Allah's forgiveness for killing a disbeliever? The answer: He was not given permission to kill him, and that is why, on the Day of Resurrection, Moses (u) will say: I have killed a soul without permission [from Allah]. Ibn Juzay: 2/141.\nWhy did Moses (u) ask for Allah's forgiveness for killing a disbeliever?\nقَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي ظَلَمۡتُ نَفۡسِي فَٱغۡفِرۡ لِي فَغَفَرَ لَهُۥٓۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ١٦\nMoses (u) regretted striking his fist that ended a human life. His regret prompted him to submit humbly to Allah, and ask for His forgiveness. Qatadah said: By Allah, he knew the way out, and sought Allah’s forgiveness, then he continued to remind himself of his sin despite knowing that he was forgiven, and even on the Day of Resurrection, he will say, \"I have killed a soul without permission [from Allah].\" So, he considered it a sin, and says, (I have wronged myself, so forgive me), since a Prophet should not kill unless he was commanded to do so, and Prophets are more conscious of their actions than others. Al-Qurtubi: 16/247-248.\nMoses considered himself responsible for killing the Egyptian. Why?\nقَالَ رَبِّ بِمَآ أَنۡعَمۡتَ عَلَيَّ فَلَنۡ أَكُونَ ظَهِيرٗا لِّلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ ١٧\nMeaning: Because of Your favor upon me, I will not help criminals. This was a covenant that Moses made with his Lord. Ibn Juzay: 2/140.\nWhat must the believer do when he commits a sin, then saw Allah's favor of keeping his action hidden from others?\nwords\nمِن شِيعَتِهِOne of his own people, the Israelites\nفَوَكَزَهُHe struck him with his fist\nيَتَرَقَّبُAnticipating trouble\nيَستَصرِخُهُHe cries out to him for help\nلَغَوِيٌّA persistent deviator"],[388,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nExtend a helping hand to someone in need.\nShare a message in which you advise women of concealing their adornments, and enjoin modesty on them, for it has always been the attribute of believing women since ancient times.\nRewarding someone who did good to you is a quality of the righteous.\nguid\nModesty (shyness) for women is a virtue, and honored believing women are those who abstain from mixing with men.\nCaring for the weak, and taking care of their interests is an trait of the Prophets (p).\nOne of the reasons for a supplication being answered is the servant's humility and his display of submissiveness as Moses (u) said:\nrefl\nقَالَ مَا خَطۡبُكُمَاۖ قَالَتَا لَا نَسۡقِي حَتَّىٰ يُصۡدِرَ ٱلرِّعَآءُۖ وَأَبُونَا شَيۡخٞ كَبِيرٞ ٢٣\n(They said, \"We do not water until the shepherds dispatch their flocks\"), we are two women, and cannot crowd with men. (And our father is an old man) who cannot attend to this matter, nor could he water his flocks, hence we wait until after people finished so we can water an leave. Al-Tabari: 19/554.\nThe verse indicates that preventing the mixing between men and women is the way of Prophets and righteous people. Explain.\nفَسَقَىٰ لَهُمَا ثُمَّ تَوَلَّىٰٓ إِلَى ٱلظِّلِّ فَقَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي لِمَآ أَنزَلۡتَ إِلَيَّ مِنۡ خَيۡرٖ فَقِيرٞ ٢٤\nAllah bestowed much good upon Moses (u); the first of which was giving him wisdom and knowledge, saving him from being killed [as a child], raising him in a royal setting, and protecting him from the religious convictions of the royal family in which he was raised, hence he benefited from its best and evaded its worst. Moreover, other types of good was making him the deliverer of his people [the Israelites], saving him again from being killed unjustly, guiding him to a faraway shelter, and made him acquainted with a family of a Prophet. Ibn Ashur: 20/102.\nMention three types of good that Allah bestowed upon His servant Moses.\nفَجَآءَتۡهُ إِحۡدَىٰهُمَا تَمۡشِي عَلَى ٱسۡتِحۡيَآءٖ قَالَتۡ إِنَّ أَبِي يَدۡعُوكَ لِيَجۡزِيَكَ أَجۡرَ مَا سَقَيۡتَ لَنَاۚ\n(Walking modestly), her modesty was natural since she was tasked with coming to a complete stranger to talk and walk with him. Al-Biqai: 14/268.\nModesty is a reason for selecting a righteous person to marry. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالَتۡ إِحۡدَىٰهُمَا يَٰٓأَبَتِ ٱسۡتَـٔۡجِرۡهُۖ إِنَّ خَيۡرَ مَنِ ٱسۡتَـٔۡجَرۡتَ ٱلۡقَوِيُّ ٱلۡأَمِينُ ٢٦\n(Hire him), let him work for you. (Indeed, the best one you can hire is the strong and the trustworthy): This is a complete wisdom, stated eloquently. It is said that her father asked: How did you know about his strength and trustworthiness? She replied: As for his strength, he lifted the stone off the top of the well, and as for his trustworthiness, he never looked at me. Ibn Juzay: 2/143.\nThis verse encourages providing advice to those in authority. Explain.\nإِنَّ خَيۡرَ مَنِ ٱسۡتَـٔۡجَرۡتَ ٱلۡقَوِيُّ ٱلۡأَمِينُ ٢٦\nThese two characteristics should be taken into account when hiring anyone to do work, because problems only arise when one or both of these characteristics is lacking. But if they are combined, then the work will be done properly. Al-Saadi: 614.\nHow do we infer from this verse the ideal traits of those who run public affairs?\nوَمَآ أُرِيدُ أَنۡ أَشُقَّ عَلَيۡكَۚ سَتَجِدُنِيٓ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ٢٧\nHe encouraged him by stating that the work would be easy and that he would treat him well. This indicates that the righteous man should have a good attitude as much as he can. Al-Saadi: 615.\nThis verse points to the manners required of business people. How?\nسَتَجِدُنِيٓ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ٢٧\nHe wanted to affirm his good manners to Moses. This is not considered self-praise, which is forbidden, since its aim is self-conceit and bragging. However, if the aim is showing goodwill in religious or dealing matters, then it is for a good cause. Ibn Ashur: 20/109.\nThe old man says, (You will find me, if Allah wills, from among the righteous). Is this self-praise?\nwords\nتِلقَاءَ مَديَنَToward the city of Madyan\nسَوَاءَ السَّبِيلِThe best way to the city of Madyan\nتَذُودَانِHolding back their flocks from water\nمَا خَطبُكُمَاWhat is your circumstance?\nيُصدِرَ الرِّعَاءُThe shepherds dispatch their flocks\nتَأجُرَنِيYou serve me as a shepherd\nحِجَجٍYears"],[389,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nConfide your worrisome and fear to Allah only, following the example of Moses in his complaint to his Lord.\nHelp a preacher with something he needs.\nSeek the help of someone, with the appropriate qualifications, to support you in calling others to Allah.\nguid\nProphets are faithful; Moses fulfilled the more complete of the two terms, which was ten years.\nAmong the traits of the righteous are working to earn a living, and the resolution of worldly problems with wisdom and patience.\nMake sure to include relevant proofs and examples in your preaching.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّآ أَتَىٰهَا نُودِيَ مِن شَٰطِيِٕ ٱلۡوَادِ ٱلۡأَيۡمَنِ فِي ٱلۡبُقۡعَةِ ٱلۡمُبَٰرَكَةِ مِنَ ٱلشَّجَرَةِ أَن يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنِّيٓ أَنَا ٱللَّهُ رَبُّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٣٠\n(The Lord of the worlds) indicates that all created beings are subjugated to Him, in order to keep firm the heart of Moses (u) against the intensity of receiving the Message.Ibn Ashur: 20/112.\nWhat is the indication of this attribute: (The Lord of the worlds)?\nوَأَنۡ أَلۡقِ عَصَاكَۚ فَلَمَّا رَءَاهَا تَهۡتَزُّ كَأَنَّهَا جَآنّٞ وَلَّىٰ مُدۡبِرٗا وَلَمۡ يُعَقِّبۡۚ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ أَقۡبِلۡ وَلَا تَخَفۡۖ إِنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلۡأٓمِنِينَ ٣١\nBut there was another possibility, which was that he could come back unafraid, but then, he might not be protected or safe from harm. Hence Allah said: (you are perfectly safe). Thus, he was completely protected in all ways. So, Moses came back, without fear; rather, he was reassured and trusted what his Lord had told him, having increased in faith and certainty. This was a sign that Allah showed him before he went to Pharaoh in order that he would have complete certainty, which would give him more courage, strength, and firmness. Al-Saadi: 615.\nHearts' fear and security are at the Hand of Allah. Explain in view of this verse.\nوَأَخِي هَٰرُونُ هُوَ أَفۡصَحُ مِنِّي لِسَانٗا فَأَرۡسِلۡهُ مَعِيَ رِدۡءٗا يُصَدِّقُنِيٓۖ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ ٣٤\nMoses did not ask for just any helper, rather, he specified his brother (Aaron), since he knew his trustworthiness, sincerity to Allah, loyalty to his brother, and his eloquent speech. Ibn Ashur: 20/116.\nAmong Prophets ways, is selecting a companion with the right traits to help in preaching to others. Explain in view of this verse.\nوَأَخِي هَٰرُونُ هُوَ أَفۡصَحُ مِنِّي لِسَانٗا فَأَرۡسِلۡهُ مَعِيَ رِدۡءٗا يُصَدِّقُنِيٓۖ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ ٣٤\n(So send him with me as a helper, to confirm my words), for that will help to make the truth clearer. Allah answered his request and said: (We will strengthen you through your brother), We will help you by means of him. Al-Saadi: 615.\nA truthful preacher will do his utmost to complete his task by all necessary means. Explain in view of this verse.\nقَالَ سَنَشُدُّ عَضُدَكَ بِأَخِيكَ\nOne of the righteous predecessors said, \"There is no one who has ever done a greater favor to his brother than what Moses did for Aaron (p), for he interceded for him until Allah made him a Prophet and Messenger with him to Pharaoh and his chiefs. Ibn Kathir: 3/375.\nMoses did a great favor for his brother Aaron (p). Explain.\nوَنَجۡعَلُ لَكُمَا سُلۡطَٰنٗا فَلَا يَصِلُونَ إِلَيۡكُمَا بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآۚ أَنتُمَا وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَكُمَا ٱلۡغَٰلِبُونَ ٣٥\n(You and your followers will prevail). This was a promise to Moses at that time, when he was alone and had returned to his homeland after having been expelled. Matters continued to develop, and unfold until Allah fulfilled his promise, gave him power over the people and the land, and he and his followers prevailed. Al-Saadi: 615.\nWhat was the benefit of this sign to Moses (u) before sending him to Pharaoh?\nقَالَ سَنَشُدُّ عَضُدَكَ بِأَخِيكَ وَنَجۡعَلُ لَكُمَا سُلۡطَٰنٗا فَلَا يَصِلُونَ إِلَيۡكُمَا بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآۚ أَنتُمَا وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَكُمَا ٱلۡغَٰلِبُونَ ٣٥\nThe lesson from this part of the story is to establish that the Message is a blessing from Allah Who reveals it upon whomever He wills among his servants. Muhammad's (ﷺ) message, just like Moses', it came to him without notice. Muhammad was called upon in the cave of Mount Hira just like Moses was called upon on the side of Mount Tur, he felt fear just like Moses did, and Allah made him firm like He did Moses, and Allah would protect him from his enemies like He protected Moses. Ibn Ashur: 20/118.\nThis verse indicates that Allah will help and make firm His Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ). Explain.\nwords\nآنَسَHe spotted\nجَذوَةٍA brand of fire\nتَصطَلُونَYou warm yourselves\nشَاطِئِA side\nفَذَانِكَThese are two\nرِدءًاA helper\nسَنَشُدُّ عَضُدَكَWe will strengthen you"],[390,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah against arrogance toward the truth.\nShare a message in which you warn those who set a bad example that they will bear their burden and that of whoever emulates him.\nAsk Allah, the Almighty, to make you a leader in goodness, and seek refuge with Him from becoming a leader in evil.\nguid\nThe believer trusts Allah's promise of best abode in the end for his obedient servants.\nBeware of being a wrongdoer, for their consequence will be a loss.\nThe consequence of wrongdoers is destruction and obliteration.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُم مُّوسَىٰ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا بَيِّنَٰتٖ قَالُواْ مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّا سِحۡرٞ مُّفۡتَرٗى وَمَا سَمِعۡنَا بِهَٰذَا فِيٓ ءَابَآئِنَا ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ٣٦\n(We have not heard of this), we never heard about what you are saying concerning the message from Allah. (Our earlier ancestors), they referred to the innovative act that misguided most people, which is following their ancient ancestors blindly, and considering that as the rule by which they judge all things. Al-Biqai: 14/292.\nReligious innovators often repeat one argument for their innovations. What is it?\nوَقَالَ فِرۡعَوۡنُ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلۡمَلَأُ مَا عَلِمۡتُ لَكُم مِّنۡ إِلَٰهٍ غَيۡرِي فَأَوۡقِدۡ لِي يَٰهَٰمَٰنُ عَلَى ٱلطِّينِ فَٱجۡعَل لِّي صَرۡحٗا لَّعَلِّيٓ أَطَّلِعُ إِلَىٰٓ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ وَإِنِّي لَأَظُنُّهُۥ مِنَ ٱلۡكَٰذِبِينَ ٣٨\nBut what is amazing about these eminent ones who claimed to be senior figures in the kingdom and running its affairs was the way in which this man toyed with their minds, and belittled their intelligence. This was because of their evildoing that was deeply entrenched in their character. Hence, their religious concepts became corrupt, which was followed by the corruption of their way of thinking. Al-Saadi: 616.\nHow did the minds of Pharaoh’s people become corrupt?\nفَٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٤٠\nSo, see O Muhammad, with your heart how those who wronged themselves, denied their Lord, and rejected His Messenger's advice -have not We destroyed them, and caused our allies to inherit their dwellings and wealth. Al-Tabari: 19/582.\nAllah enjoined His Prophet (ﷺ) to see how was the destruction of Pharaoh and his soldiers, even though he was not there at the time. Explain.\nوَجَعَلۡنَٰهُمۡ أَئِمَّةٗ يَدۡعُونَ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِۖ وَيَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ لَا يُنصَرُونَ ٤١\n(Leaders inviting to the Fire), they were calling people to the disbelief that leads them to Hellfire. Ibn Juzay: 2/143.\nHow can someone be a leader inviting to Hellfire?\nوَجَعَلۡنَٰهُمۡ أَئِمَّةٗ يَدۡعُونَ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِۖ وَيَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ لَا يُنصَرُونَ ٤١\nMeaning: We made them chiefs leading others to disbelief, and they will bear their burden of sins besides that of their followers, hence, their punishment will be much more. It is said that Allah made the eminent ones leaders to the lowest among them, hence, they call to Hellfire. Moreover, it is said that they were made leaders so that discerning people would be admonished by their demise. Al-Qurtubi: 16/330.\nExplain how they were leaders in disbelief.\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَى ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَآ أَهۡلَكۡنَا ٱلۡقُرُونَ ٱلۡأُولَىٰ بَصَآئِرَ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٗ لَّعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٤٣\nBefore revealing the Torah, Allah's way of taking retribution from nations who denied their Prophets was to afflict them with a punishment from Himself; as He destroyed Noah's people by drowning, Hūd's people by violent wind, Salih's people by huge blast, Shu'ayb's people by fiery clouds, Lot's people by a storm of stones, and Pharaoh's people by drowning. Ibn Taimyah: 5/80.\nMention five types of Allah's punishments on disobedient nations.\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَى ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَآ أَهۡلَكۡنَا ٱلۡقُرُونَ ٱلۡأُولَىٰ\nThis indicates that after the revelation of the Torah, the full destruction of nations ceased, and Jihad against the disbelievers with the sword was prescribed. Al-Saadi: 617.\nWas there any total destruction of any nation after that of Pharaoh and his people?\nwords\nمُفتَرىًFabricated lies about Allah\nعَاقِبَةُ الدَّارِThe best abode in the Hereafter\nصَرحًاA high rise building, tower\nفَنَبَذنَاهُم فِي اليَمِّWe threw them into the sea\nأَئِمَّةًLeaders to Hellfire\nوَأَتبَعنَاهُمAnd We caused to overtake them\nالمَقبُوحِينَThey will be despised\nبَصَائِرَ لِلنَّاسِEnlightenment for the people to see the truth"],[391,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nSelect a story from the Quran, and read about it from interpretation or history books, as it has lessons and admonishments.\nIdentify a deed in which you followed your desire instead of Allah's Sharia, then ask for Allah's forgiveness, and follow Allah's Sharia instead.\nSeek refuge with Allah from following desires, and from going astray after guidance.\nguid\nKeeping up with faith and knowledge is required, since old age and passage of time cause forgetfulness.\nThe Muslim acts upon the authentic proof of Sharia.\nKnow that there is no book contains more guidance than Allah's Book [the Quran].\nrefl\nوَمَا كُنتَ بِجَانِبِ ٱلۡغَرۡبِيِّ إِذۡ قَضَيۡنَآ إِلَىٰ مُوسَى ٱلۡأَمۡرَ وَمَا كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ ٤٤\n(You were not on the western side), this is addressed to our Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ), in order to affirm his absence from Moses’ situation, yet he is informed about it. (The western): Is the western side of Mount Tur at which Allah spoke to Moses, and the command was Prophethood. (Nor did you witness that event), you were not present there; meaning: You did not attend there in order to witness all these unknown events that We inform you about, but their news came to you through Our revelation. Hence, people must hasten to believe in your Prophethood. Ibn Juzay: 2/145.\nThe story of Moses (ﷺ) is proof that this Quran is from Allah and that Muhammad is His Messenger. How?\nوَلَٰكِنَّآ أَنشَأۡنَا قُرُونٗا فَتَطَاوَلَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡعُمُرُۚ وَمَا كُنتَ ثَاوِيٗا فِيٓ أَهۡلِ مَدۡيَنَ تَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا وَلَٰكِنَّا كُنَّا مُرۡسِلِينَ ٤٥\nKnowledge vanished, and Allah's revelations were forgotten. Then We sent you at a time when there was a great need for you, and for that which We have taught you and revealed to you. Al-Saadi: 617.\nWhen is the time the presence of a preacher is most needed to remind and teach people?\nوَلَٰكِنَّآ أَنشَأۡنَا قُرُونٗا فَتَطَاوَلَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡعُمُرُۚ وَمَا كُنتَ ثَاوِيٗا فِيٓ أَهۡلِ مَدۡيَنَ تَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا وَلَٰكِنَّا كُنَّا مُرۡسِلِينَ ٤٥\nAllah took covenants from Moses and his people to believe and support Muhammad (ﷺ), but after a long time passed on them, and generations succeeded one another, they forgot these covenants and failed to keep them. Al-Baghawi: 3/443.\nWhat did Moses' people forget after a long time passed on them?\nوَلَوۡلَآ أَن تُصِيبَهُم مُّصِيبَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ\nMeaning: For the disbelief and sins that they committed. All deeds are attributed to the hands, since most of the are, even if some are not committed by hands. Al-Alusi: 10/297.\nHands are a blessing from Allah, which can be used for good and evil. Explain.\nفَإِن لَّمۡ يَسۡتَجِيبُواْ لَكَ فَٱعۡلَمۡ أَنَّمَا يَتَّبِعُونَ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡۚ وَمَنۡ أَضَلُّ مِمَّنِ ٱتَّبَعَ هَوَىٰهُ بِغَيۡرِ هُدٗى مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٥٠\nThis indicates that anyone who does not respond to the Messenger (ﷺ), but follows a view contrary to that of the Messenger (ﷺ), then, he is not following true guidance; rather he is following whims and desires. Al-Saadi: 618.\nWhat is the sign of following desires, which is mentioned in this verse?\nفَإِن لَّمۡ يَسۡتَجِيبُواْ لَكَ فَٱعۡلَمۡ أَنَّمَا يَتَّبِعُونَ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡۚ وَمَنۡ أَضَلُّ مِمَّنِ ٱتَّبَعَ هَوَىٰهُ بِغَيۡرِ هُدٗى مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٥٠\nDesires are the drives of the soul without knowledge. Hence, whoever acts upon what his soul wants without knowledge showing its benefit, is a follower of his desire. The knowledge of what is beneficial for anyone in the Hereafter is what the Messengers brought. Ibn Taimyah: 5/83.\nWhat is meant by desires that are followed by the people of falsehood?\nوَمَنۡ أَضَلُّ مِمَّنِ ٱتَّبَعَ هَوَىٰهُ بِغَيۡرِ هُدٗى مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٥٠\nFollowing desires without using reason on how to be saved will lead to infinite miseries. Ibn Ashur: 20/141.\nWhy is there no more astray than one who follows his desire?\nwords\nالغَربِيِّThe western mount from Moses (u)\nقَضَينَاWe revealed the command\nأَنشَأنَاWe brought forth\nفَتَطَاوَلَ عَلَيهِمُ العُمُرُA long time passed on them\nثَاوِيًاResiding"],[392,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nSpend some of your wealth in the way of Allah.\nAttend a circle for remembering Allah, and concentrate with your mind and ears.\nShare a message in which you warn against spending wastefully and living insolently, for these are among the reasons for the cease of blessings, and cite this verse:\nguid\nAffirming the virtue of people of the Book who believed in the unlettered Prophet, his Book [the Quran], and submitted to the Lord of the worlds.\nAffirming the virtue of those who repel evil with good, and spend from what Allah has provided for them.\nRefrain from uttering ill speech, even with disobedient people.\nrefl\n۞وَلَقَدۡ وَصَّلۡنَا لَهُمُ ٱلۡقَوۡلَ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٥١\nConveying the Quran has many ways. In terms of its verses, they were not revealed all at once, rather, they came down in segments and then were conveyed together. In terms of its meanings, there are a variety of topics conveyed, such as promise, warning, encouragement, intimidation, narrations, admonishments, lessons, and advice. All these topics come in succession, moving from one area to another, which helps the mind stay active in remembering and reflecting. Ibn Ashur: 20/142.\nExplain the aspects of conveying the Quran.\nوَيَدۡرَءُونَ بِٱلۡحَسَنَةِ ٱلسَّيِّئَةَ\nIt is said that they repel evil with endurance and good words. This is considered good morals where if someone says abusive words to them, they repel them with good words. Moreover, it is said that they repel sins with repentance and pursuit of Allah’s forgiveness. Al-Qurtubi: 16/296.\nHow is evil repelled with good?\nوَإِذَا سَمِعُواْ ٱللَّغۡوَ أَعۡرَضُواْ عَنۡهُ وَقَالُواْ لَنَآ أَعۡمَٰلُنَا وَلَكُمۡ أَعۡمَٰلُكُمۡ سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡكُمۡ لَا نَبۡتَغِي ٱلۡجَٰهِلِينَ ٥٥\nTheir saying: (we seek not the ignorant) reveals their character, in that they aspire to knowledge and good morals. Ibn Juzay: 20/146.\nThe people of the Scripture who believed in the Quran say, (we seek not the ignorant). What is the indication of that?\nسَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡكُمۡ لَا نَبۡتَغِي ٱلۡجَٰهِلِينَ ٥٥\n(Peace will be upon you), keeping off and staying away, rather than greeting; it is a greeting for parting. (We seek not the ignorant), we do not seek argument with them. Al-Alusi: 10/297.\nWhat should a Muslim do when he is in a place of ill speech and falsehood?\nإِنَّكَ لَا تَهۡدِي مَنۡ أَحۡبَبۡتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَهۡدِي مَن يَشَآءُۚ وَهُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِٱلۡمُهۡتَدِينَ ٥٦\nIt is said that the guidance of the heart can only be granted by Allah. However, the servant can attain the means for guidance, which is required of him in saying: (Guide us to the straight path), and Allah precluded the Messenger (ﷺ) from affecting this guidance by saying: (You do not guide whom you like). Ibn Taimyah: 5/87.\nWhat is meant by the guidance that only Allah can grant?\nوَقَالُوٓاْ إِن نَّتَّبِعِ ٱلۡهُدَىٰ مَعَكَ نُتَخَطَّفۡ مِنۡ أَرۡضِنَآۚ أَوَ لَمۡ نُمَكِّن لَّهُمۡ حَرَمًا ءَامِنٗا يُجۡبَىٰٓ إِلَيۡهِ ثَمَرَٰتُ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ رِّزۡقٗا مِّن لَّدُنَّا وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٥٧\nThere was no basis for fearing being snatched away if they believed in Allah since they did not fear the same while they were worshiping idols. How could they fear when they add the sanctity of faith to that of the holy place?! Al-Alusi: 10/305.\nTrue security lies in guidance and following Allah’s Sharia. Explain.\nوَكَمۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَا مِن قَرۡيَةِۢ بَطِرَتۡ مَعِيشَتَهَاۖ فَتِلۡكَ مَسَٰكِنُهُمۡ لَمۡ تُسۡكَن مِّنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗاۖ وَكُنَّا نَحۡنُ ٱلۡوَٰرِثِينَ ٥٨\nThey were insolent in their way of life to the point of excessive play and diversion, hence, they corrupted the blessings in their life, and were not grateful for them. Rather, became bewildered with them and did not take good care of them. Al-Biqai: 14/327.\nWhen can a luxury life be a cause for destruction?\nwords\nوَصَّلنَاWe detailed\nمَرَّتَينِTwice, [they will be rewarded twice due to their belief in their Book and the Quran]\nوَيَدرَأُونَThey repel\nنُتَخَطَّفWe will be snatched away\nبَطِرَت مَعِيشَتَهَاIt was insolent in its way of living"],[393,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him today as many as seventy times.\nBefore embarking on any of your worldly matters, pray two Rak'as for seeking guidance, then say this supplication: \"O Allah, I seek Your counsel by Your knowledge, and by Your power I seek strength, and I ask You from Your great blessings, for verily You are able while I am not able, and verily You know while I do not know, and indeed You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if You know that this affair -and here he mentions his need- is good for me in relation to my religion, my life, and final end, then decree it, ease it for me, and bless me with it. If You know that this affair is evil for me toward my religion, my life, and end, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, and decree for me what is good wherever it be, and make me content with that.\"\nAsk Allah to make you righteous inwardly and outwardly.\nguid\nDo not be distracted by food, cloths, or a house in this world from what will be in the Hereafter.\nThe leaders of misguidance will disown their followers on the Day of Resurrection.\nWhen you fined an authentic proof on any religious matter, then follow and adhere to it, and remember that Allah will ask you: What did you answer the messenger?\nrefl\nوَمَآ أُوتِيتُم مِّن شَيۡءٖ فَمَتَٰعُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَزِينَتُهَاۚ وَمَا عِندَ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ وَأَبۡقَىٰٓۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ٦٠\n(Is only an enjoyment and adornment of the life of this world), it is a temporary enjoyment for a short time. The words: (enjoyment and adornment of the life of this world) imply insignificance, as opposed to the words describing the reward in the Hereafter, which are: (what is with Allah is better and more lasting); these words imply pure joy, perfect delight, and everlasting. (Will you not then understand), do you not see the difference between what lasts forever and what will come to an end? But, you do not make the obvious choice, and thus, exchange what is better for what is less. Al-Alusi: 10/306.\nThis verse points to the insignificance of this worldly life compared to the Hereafter. Explain\nوَمَآ أُوتِيتُم مِّن شَيۡءٖ فَمَتَٰعُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَزِينَتُهَاۚ وَمَا عِندَ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ وَأَبۡقَىٰٓۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ٦٠\nThis indicates that the more rational a person is, the more he will give precedence to the Hereafter over this world, and no one gives precedence to this world unless there is a deficiency in his reasoning. Al-Saadi: 621.\nHow do you differentiate between a rational person and a non-rational one?\nوَمَآ أُوتِيتُم مِّن شَيۡءٖ فَمَتَٰعُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَزِينَتُهَاۚ وَمَا عِندَ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ وَأَبۡقَىٰٓۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ٦٠\nMeaning: What is with Allah for His obedient servants and allies is much better than what you have been given of enjoyment and adornment in this worldly life. Al-Tabari: 19/604.\nMost of the adornments of this worldly life are given to the disbelievers. Why?\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ حَقَّ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡقَوۡلُ رَبَّنَا هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ ٱلَّذِينَ أَغۡوَيۡنَآ أَغۡوَيۡنَٰهُمۡ كَمَا غَوَيۡنَاۖ تَبَرَّأۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَۖ مَا كَانُوٓاْ إِيَّانَا يَعۡبُدُونَ ٦٣\n(Our Lord, these are the ones), pointing to their followers. (Whom we led astray), we misguided them by making our words, which were fallible and wrong, appealing to them because of our power and wealth. Then they will say what they think will exonerate them: (We led them astray as we ourselves went astray), their followers chose misguidance. Al-Biqai: 14/334.\nIn view of this verse, explain the risk of bad companions and following them blindly.\nوَيَوۡمَ يُنَادِيهِمۡ فَيَقُولُ مَاذَآ أَجَبۡتُمُ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٦٥ فَعَمِيَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡأَنۢبَآءُ يَوۡمَئِذٖ فَهُمۡ لَا يَتَسَآءَلُونَ ٦٦\nMeaning: They will not be able to find any argument for themselves since Allah has left them with no excuse or information to evade the punishment. Al-Tabari: 19/607.\nThe disobedient will not find any argument for them on the Day of Resurrection. Why?\nفَأَمَّا مَن تَابَ وَءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا فَعَسَىٰٓ أَن يَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحِينَ ٦٧\nWhen this term: (Perhaps) is used in reference to Allah, it implies that the thing described will inevitably come to pass, and this will undoubtedly happen by the grace and mercy of Allah. Ibn Kathir: 3/383.\nWhat does the term: (Perhaps) imply when it is used in reference to Allah?\nوَرَبُّكَ يَخۡلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيَخۡتَارُۗ مَا كَانَ لَهُمُ ٱلۡخِيَرَةُۚ\nSome scholars said: No Muslim should embark on any worldly matter until he asks for Allah's guidance by praying two Rak'as for seeking guidance. Al-Qurtubi: 16/308\nHow do you attain guidance from Allah for your worldly matters?\nwords\nأَغوَينَاWe called them to misguidance and they followed us\nفَعَمِيَتIt will become unapparent\nالخِيَرَةُThe choice"],[394,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nRecall a success you have achieved, and thank Allah, and stand humble before Him.\nSleep early tonight and wake up early, as this is a way to give thanks to Allah, and is closer to human nature.\nMake a schedule of your monthly income in which you balance your worldly interests and that of the Hereafter.\nguid\nTrue listening is the that of the heart and its responsiveness.\nWorking to earn a living during the day and resting during the night, while avoiding anything that displeases Allah, is a form of expressing gratitude to Him.\nWhoever does not accept and believe in Islam today, will learn the truth when he stands before Allah, the Almighty.\nrefl\nقُلۡ أَرَءَيۡتُمۡ إِن جَعَلَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلَّيۡلَ سَرۡمَدًا إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ مَنۡ إِلَٰهٌ غَيۡرُ ٱللَّهِ يَأۡتِيكُم بِضِيَآءٍۚ أَفَلَا تَسۡمَعُونَ ٧١\nThis recurrent amazing creation that occurs twice daily is an excellent inference of the Oneness of Allah. Every sane person is well aware of its occurrence; it is one of the most evident manifestations of change in this universe. Ibn Ashur: 20/168.\nInference of the Oneness of Allah here is based on the alternation of day and night. Why?\nقُلۡ أَرَءَيۡتُمۡ إِن جَعَلَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلَّيۡلَ سَرۡمَدًا إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ مَنۡ إِلَٰهٌ غَيۡرُ ٱللَّهِ يَأۡتِيكُم بِضِيَآءٍۚ أَفَلَا تَسۡمَعُونَ ٧١\nIn these verses, Allah points out that the individual should reflect on the blessings that Allah has bestowed upon him, try to understand them and compare what he has with what his situation would be if he did not have those blessings. If he compares his situation when he has these blessings and what it would be if he did not have them, he will become more aware of the great blessings that he has, unlike the one who thinks of them as nothing out of the ordinary and thinks that he will always have them, and thus is no longer appreciative of the blessings of Allah, and does not realize his need for these blessings at all times. Al-Saadi: 623.\nThe verses point to a case for reflection on Allah's blessings. What is it?\nوَمِن رَّحۡمَتِهِۦ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلَّيۡلَ وَٱلنَّهَارَ لِتَسۡكُنُواْ فِيهِ وَلِتَبۡتَغُواْ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦ وَلَعَلَّكُمۡ تَشۡكُرُونَ ٧٣\nAllah specifies resting during the night and working during the day, since that is the most common setting for people, even if some rest during the day and work during the night, but that is a negligible exception to the rule. Ibn Atiyah: 4/297.\nSome people rest during the day and work during the night. Does that contradict the verse? Explain.\nإِنَّ قَٰرُونَ كَانَ مِن قَوۡمِ مُوسَىٰ فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡۖ\nWhen Allah says, (And whatever you have been given is only an enjoyment and adornment of the life of this world), He revealed that Korah was given all that, and he became deluded by it, but it did not save him from Allah's punishment as it did not save Pharaoh. As for you, O polytheists, you do not actually have the men and wealth that Korah and Pharoh had, yet Pharaoh's soldiers did not avail him, nor did Korah's treasures or his kinship ties to Moses (u). Al-Qurtubi: 16/312.\nAllah narrates Korah's story. Why? What is the lesson to be learned from that?\nإِذۡ قَالَ لَهُۥ قَوۡمُهُۥ لَا تَفۡرَحۡۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡفَرِحِينَ ٧٦\n(Do not exult), the exultation that leads to self-admiration and tyranny, and that is why Allah says, (Allah does not like the exultant). Moreover, it is said that it means rejoicing over this life’s gains, since only those who are heedless of the Hereafter do that. This meaning is indicated by this verse: (Nor rejoice over that which has been given to you) [57:23]. Ibn Juzay: 2/151.\nWhat is the prohibited exultation?\nوَلَا تَنسَ نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ وَأَحۡسِن كَمَآ أَحۡسَنَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيۡكَۖ\nMeaning: Do not neglect your share of your world, rather, enjoy it while working for the Hereafter. It is said that it means do not waste your life by neglecting to do righteous deeds, as a man’s share of this world is the good deeds he makes. Hence, based on this interpretation, the statement becomes an admonishment. As for the first interpretation, it makes it lawful to enjoy life, lest the listener becomes turned off by the admonishment. (And do good as Allah has done good to you), do good as Allah has done good to you by giving you wealth. Ibn Juzay: 2/151.\nHow can the servant be saved from the trial of wealth in this worldly life?\nوَلَا تَنسَ نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ\nAttributing the share to the listener indicates that it is within his right to enjoy his wealth in a way that is suitable to him, especially if it is not spent in Allah's cause, as long as it is not prohibited. Ibn Ashur: 20/179.\nThe Muslim should not restrict his spending on eating or drinking while he is wealthy. Explain.\nwords\nسَرمَدًاPerpetual\nوَضَلَّLost\nيَفتَرُونَWhat they used to invent\nلَتَنُوءُ بِالعُصبَةِIt would burden a band of strong men\nوَابتَغِSeek\nوَلاَ تَنسَ نَصِيبَكَDo not abandon your share"],[395,"§Al-Qasas\ndeeds\nAdvise an acquaintance of yours, who is deluded by appearances, that worldly adornments will come to an end, and remind him of Korah’s story.\nSit down with a poor laborer, find out about his needs, and give him charity .\nSeek refuge with Allah from arrogance and spreading corruption on earth.\nguid\nTemptation is quicker to the hearts of greedy worldly people.\nWhen a trial comes, only the scholars know it, but after it passes, all people know it.\nIt is the grace and mercy of Allah that He multiplies good deeds and does not multiply bad ones.\nrefl\nقَالَ إِنَّمَآ أُوتِيتُهُۥ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمٍ عِندِيٓۚ أَوَ لَمۡ يَعۡلَمۡ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ قَدۡ أَهۡلَكَ مِن قَبۡلِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلۡقُرُونِ مَنۡ هُوَ أَشَدُّ مِنۡهُ قُوَّةٗ وَأَكۡثَرُ جَمۡعٗاۚ\nMeaning: Did he not know the benefit of knowledge? Was he not aware of how Allah punished those who were much more powerful than him, in a physical and moral sense, and had more wealth or people around them and at their service, lest he become deluded like they did? Al-Alusi: 10/326.\nWhat is Allah's way of dealing with those who are deluded by their power or wealth?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ وَيۡلَكُمۡ ثَوَابُ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ لِّمَنۡ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗاۚ\n(Those who had been given knowledge said), they knew the reality of this life and the Hereafter. They did not describe the reward as: \"reward of the Hereafter\" to indicate that the true knowledge about this worldly life and the Hereafter would necessitate turning away from the former and seeking the latter. Hence, the yearning of those who wished was due to their lack of proper knowledge about this worldly life and the Hereafter. Al-Alusi: 10/327.\nWhoever, knowingly, turns away from this worldly life and seeks the Hereafter, will be more steadfast than others during trials. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ وَيۡلَكُمۡ ثَوَابُ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ لِّمَنۡ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗاۚ\nThose (who had been given knowledge) did not wish ill for those who desired the worldly life, because lenient speech was more suitable for admonishment, rather, they were astounded at their attachment to the adornments of worldly life, their fascination with Korah's status while knowing his ungodly behavior, and their disregard of Allah's reward that they could attain through adhering to their religion and doing good deeds. Ibn Ashur: 20/184.\nThose who had been given knowledge said: (Woe to you!). What did they mean?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ وَيۡلَكُمۡ ثَوَابُ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ لِّمَنۡ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗاۚ وَلَا يُلَقَّىٰهَآ إِلَّا ٱلصَّٰبِرُونَ ٨٠\n(Except the patient), those who refrained patiently from seeking the adornments of worldly life, and preferred Allah's reward for righteous deeds over worldly desires and pleasures, hence, they hastened to the obedience of Allah and disdained worldly life. Al-Tabari: 19/629.\nWho is given steadfastness during times of trials?\nوَلَا يُلَقَّىٰهَآ إِلَّا ٱلصَّٰبِرُونَ ٨٠\n(And none are granted it), none would be willing to accept and abide by the words of those who had been given knowledge (except the patient), who endure patiently with their Lord’s decrees in times of prosperity and adversity, and bring themselves to obeying Allah. Patience has become a trait for them, and they are referred to in plural to indicate collaboration since religious acts are better performed in congregation. Al-Biqai: 14/358.\nPatience is a great trait which requires collaboration. How is this meaning inferred form the verse?\nفَخَسَفۡنَا بِهِۦ وَبِدَارِهِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ\nAs a requital that matched his deed, for he had put himself above the servants of Allah, therefore, Allah brought him to the lowest of the low, him and the things by which he had been deluded, namely his house, furnishings and other possessions. Al-Saadi: 624.\nWhy was Korah punished in this manner?\nتِلۡكَ ٱلدَّارُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةُ نَجۡعَلُهَا لِلَّذِينَ لَا يُرِيدُونَ عُلُوّٗا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَا فَسَادٗاۚ\nIn Surat Al-Qasas, Allah begins by mentioning Pharaoh's exaltedness through governance and authority, and at the end of the Surah, He mentions Korah's corruption through great wealth, then He indicates the consequence of Pharaoh's authority, and Korah’s wealth, saying: (That is the abode of the Hereafter We will assign to those who neither seek exaltedness nor corruption on earth), similar to the situation of Pharaoh and Korah. Ibn Taimyah: 5/90.\nThe Surah ends with mentioning two traits of the people of Paradise who neither seek exaltedness nor corruption on earth. Why?\nwords\nالقُرُونِNations, generations\nوَلاَ يُسأَلُThey will not be asked for information, rather as a form of censure and rebuke\nوَيكَأَنَّA word to express astonishment and sorrow\nوَيكَأَنَّهُDid you not know\nعُلُوًّاArrogance"]])